;; expect: Bool.or refused name_taken
;; §8.4 slice 3.25 rule 2: Init's names are Init's. The module `Bool` declares `or`, the name
;; of an Init constant (line 182,994 of the export); where the environment holds that
;; constant — this test's one load of the whole export, the release gate — the declaration
;; is refused by name, since K admits no second constant under a name (already_declared).
;; A driver whose lazy stream stopped before it accepts the file (define_test.sh loads it
;; so, through Int.decEq): §8.4 slice 3.19's finding stands there — a row of the realization
;; registry speaks for Init's constant, never for a native declaration bearing its name, so
;; `f` is the call of the native `or` (K decides `f true true = false`), not the row's
;; `(if a true b)`; the gate refuses what the driver let through.
(import "Bool.shard")
(import Init Int.decEq)
(fn f ((a Bool) (b Bool)) Bool (Bool.or a b))
(theorem f_is_native () (= (f Bool.true Bool.true) Bool.false) (exact (Eq.refl Bool.false)))
